    <note class="self-check" id="note-00001">
      <exercise id="exer-00008">
        <problem id="prob-00017">
          <para id="para-00059"><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_4_4_3_SC"/></para>
        </problem>
      </exercise>
    </note>
    <section id="sect-00006">
      <title>Additional Resources</title>

      <section id="sect-00007">
        <title>Write the Function Rule from a Table</title>
        <para id="para-00066">Kelly can tune 6 cars in 3 hours. The table below is completed to show
          this relationship. The last column has the output for any <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>. This is the rule of the
          function.</para>
        <table class="unnumbered os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00004">
          <tgroup cols="6">
            <tbody>
              <row>
                <entry><emphasis> Time spent tuning cars (<m:math display="inline">
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:math>) </emphasis>
                </entry>
                <entry> 2 </entry>
                <entry> 3 </entry>
                <entry> 6 </entry>
                <entry> 7 </entry>
                <entry>
                  <m:math display="inline">
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:math>
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><emphasis> Number of cars tuned up (<m:math display="inline">
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:math>) </emphasis>
                </entry>
                <entry> 4 </entry>
                <entry> 6 </entry>
                <entry> 12 </entry>
                <entry> 14 </entry>
                <entry>
                  <m:math display="inline">
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                      <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:math>
                </entry>
              </row>
            </tbody>
          </tgroup>
        </table>

        <para id="para-00067">Kelly can tune 6 cars in 3 hours or 2 cars in 1 hour, so the function
          rule is <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>f</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>.</para>
        <note class="try" id="note-00002">
          <title>Try It: Write the Function Rule from a Table</title>
    <para id="para-00068">Determine
          the rule in function notation for the table below:</para>
    <table class="unnumbered os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00005">
            <tgroup cols="6">
              <tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry><emphasis>
                      <m:math display="inline">
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:math>
          (input) </emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry> 1 </entry>
                  <entry> 2 </entry>
                  <entry> 3 </entry>
                  <entry> 4 </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <m:math display="inline">
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:math>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry><emphasis>
                      <m:math display="inline">
                        <m:mrow>
                          <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                        </m:mrow>
                      </m:math>
          (output) </emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry> 5 </entry>
                  <entry> 8 </entry>
                  <entry> 11 </entry>
                  <entry> 14 </entry>
                  <entry> ? </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </tgroup>
          </table>
    
    <exercise id="exer-00007">
            <problem id="prob-00016">

              <para id="para-00069"></para>

            </problem>
            <solution id="sol-00016">
              <para id="para-00070">Compare your answers:</para>

              <para id="para-00071">Here is how to find the rule in function notation:</para>

              <para id="para-00072">In the table, every <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math> is multiplied
          by 3, and then 2 is added. The rule is:</para>

              <para id="para-00073"><m:math>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>f</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></para>
            </solution>
          </exercise></note>
      </section>
    </section>

  </content>
